Description: RPBridge USB multi-bus bridge kernel driver (DKMS)
 RPBridge is an open-source USB-to-multi-bus developer tool built on the
 Raspberry Pi RP2354B. The bridge exposes I²C, SPI, UART, GPIO, PWM, ADC,
 CAN 2.0B, addressable LED strips, DMX-512, 1-Wire and I²S to a Linux
 host as standard subsystem devices, usable with stock tools (i2c-tools,
 libgpiod, can-utils, spidev_test, iio_info, w1-tools).
 .
 This package ships the Linux kernel driver source and integrates it
 with DKMS so the module is rebuilt automatically on kernel upgrades.
 The driver is plain C against the stable kernel-module ABI; minimum
 kernel version is 5.15 (auxiliary_bus baseline), with CI verification
 against the 7.0 LTS kernel that ships with Ubuntu 26.04 LTS.
